## Best Practices & Style Guide

### TypeScript Best Practices

* Use **strict type checking** (`strict: true` in `tsconfig.json`).
* Prefer **type inference** when types are obvious.
* Avoid `any`; use `unknown` when a type is uncertain.
* Prefer **readonly** for immutable values.
* Use consistent formatting (Prettier + ESLint recommended ruleset).

### Angular Best Practices

* Always use **standalone components** (NgModules are deprecated in Angular 20+).
* **Do not** manually set `standalone: true` — it is now the default.
* Use **signals** for reactive state management.
* Implement **lazy loading** for feature routes.
* Use `NgOptimizedImage` for all static images (avoid inline base64 images).
* **Do not use** `@HostBinding` or `@HostListener`; use the `host` object instead.

---

## Component Guidelines

* Keep components **small and focused** on a single responsibility.
* Use `input()` and `output()` **functions** instead of decorators.
* Use `computed()` for derived or calculated state.
* Always set `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`.
* Prefer **inline templates** only for very small, purely presentational components.
* Prefer **Reactive Forms** over Template-driven Forms.
* Avoid `ngClass` and `ngStyle`; use direct `class` and `style` bindings.
* Utilize tailwind or CSS variables for theming instead of inline styles.
* Use tailwindcss for utility-first styling.

**Resources:**

* [Inputs](https://angular.dev/guide/components/inputs)
* [Outputs](https://angular.dev/guide/components/outputs)
* [Signals](https://angular.dev/guide/signals)
* [CSS & Style Bindings](https://angular.dev/guide/templates/binding#css-class-and-style-property-bindings)
* [TailwindCSS3](https://v3.tailwindcss.com/docs)
* [TailwindCSS4](https://tailwindcss.com/docs)

---

## State Management

* Use **signals** for local component state.
* Use `computed()` for derived values.
* Keep state transformations **pure and predictable**.
* Do **not** use `mutate` on signals — use `update()` or `set()`.

---

## Templates

* Keep templates **simple and declarative**.
* Use native control flow (`@if`, `@for`, `@switch`) instead of `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, `*ngSwitch`.
* Use the `async` pipe for observable bindings.
* Use built-in or imported pipes explicitly when needed.
* Avoid embedding complex business logic in templates.

**Example:**

```html
@for (item of items(); track item.id) {
  <li>{{ item.name }}</li>
}
```

---

## Services

* Follow **single responsibility** principle.
* Use `providedIn: 'root'` for singleton services.
* Prefer `inject()` over constructor injection for dependencies.
* Avoid large monolithic services; prefer smaller, focused services.

---

## Unit Testing (Jest)

* Use **Jest** for unit testing.
* Use **Angular Testing Library** for DOM interaction testing.
* Use **TestBed** utilities only when dependency injection or Angular-specific setup is required.
* Mock HTTP calls via `HttpTestingController` or service mocks.
* Test components for initialization, input/output behavior, and template rendering.

**Unit Test Example:**

```ts
import { render, screen, fireEvent } from '@testing-library/angular';
import { AppComponent } from './app.component';

describe('AppComponent', () => {
  it('should toggle server status on button click', async () => {
    await render(AppComponent);
    const button = screen.getByRole('button', { name: /toggle server status/i });
    fireEvent.click(button);
    expect(screen.getByText(/no, the server is not running/i)).toBeTruthy();
  });
});
```

---

## Integration & E2E Testing (Cypress)

* Use **Cypress** for E2E testing.
* Write tests that represent **real user flows**: navigation, form submission, API calls.
* Keep tests deterministic and independent (no hidden state between tests).
* Stub or intercept HTTP calls using `cy.intercept()`.
* Ensure accessibility testing (e.g., via `cypress-axe`).

**Example:**

```ts
describe('Server Toggle', () => {
  it('should toggle server status correctly', () => {
    cy.visit('/');
    cy.contains('Yes, the server is running');
    cy.contains('button', 'Toggle Server Status').click();
    cy.contains('No, the server is not running');
  });
});
```

